Fix AOT/trimming warnings in several files in `/tmp/sv-50571550435b46a38fb51cc79480240a/before/`. Apply the following specific fixes:

## 1. ArmEnvironment.cs - Fix `JsonSerializer.Serialize(this)` (line 80)

The struct `ArmEnvironment` has properties `Endpoint` (Uri) and `Audience` (string) and `DefaultScope` (string). Replace the `JsonSerializer.Serialize(this)` call with manual JSON construction using `JsonSerializer.SerializeToUtf8Bytes` is not AOT-safe either. Instead, manually build the JSON string:

```csharp
public override string ToString()
{
    using var stream = new System.IO.MemoryStream();
    using (var writer = new Utf8JsonWriter(stream))
    {
        writer.WriteStartObject();
        writer.WriteString("Endpoint"u8, Endpoint.AbsoluteUri);
        writer.WriteString("Audience"u8, Audience);
        writer.WriteString("DefaultScope"u8, DefaultScope);
        writer.WriteEndObject();
    }
    return System.Text.Encoding.UTF8.GetString(stream.ToArray());
}
```

Make sure to add `using System.IO;` and `using System.Text;` if not already present (check the current using statements first).

## 2. ArmClientOptions.cs - Fix `JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Dictionary<string, Dictionary<string, JsonElement>>>(span)` (line 52)

Replace with manual JsonDocument parsing. The data is a JSON object where keys map to objects which in turn map to JsonElement values. Replace:
```csharp
var allProfile = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Dictionary<string, Dictionary<string, JsonElement>>>(span);
```
with:
```csharp
using var profileDoc = JsonDocument.Parse(BinaryData.FromStream(stream));
var allProfile = new Dictionary<string, Dictionary<string, JsonElement>>();
foreach (var outerProp in profileDoc.RootElement.EnumerateObject())
{
    var innerDict = new Dictionary<string, JsonElement>();
    foreach (var innerProp in outerProp.Value.EnumerateObject())
    {
        innerDict[innerProp.Name] = innerProp.Value.Clone();
    }
    allProfile[outerProp.Name] = innerDict;
}
```

**IMPORTANT**: Note that the current code does `var span = BinaryData.FromStream(stream).ToMemory().Span;` on line 51 and then uses `span` on line 52. After the change, the `span` variable is no longer needed. Remove line 51 (`var span = ...`) and change line 52 to use the `stream` directly via `JsonDocument.Parse(BinaryData.FromStream(stream))`. Actually - you should change the overall structure so you read from the stream into a JsonDocument directly. The full replacement for lines 51-52 should be:
```csharp
using var profileDoc = JsonDocument.Parse(BinaryData.FromStream(stream));
var allProfile = new Dictionary<string, Dictionary<string, JsonElement>>();
foreach (var outerProp in profileDoc.RootElement.EnumerateObject())
{
    var innerDict = new Dictionary<string, JsonElement>();
    foreach (var innerProp in outerProp.Value.EnumerateObject())
    {
        innerDict[innerProp.Name] = innerProp.Value.Clone();
    }
    allProfile[outerProp.Name] = innerDict;
}
```

## 3. ArmOperation.cs - Fix IL2087/IL2090 (lines 96-111)

The method `IsResource<T>()` uses `typeof(T).GetConstructor(...)` and `Activator.CreateInstance(typeof(T), ...)`. Add `[DynamicallyAccessedMembers]` to the generic type parameter. The method signature at line 96 is:
```csharp
private static bool IsResource<T>() where T : notnull
```
Change to:
```csharp
private static bool IsResource<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.PublicConstructors | DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T>() where T : notnull
```

Also, add `using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;` to the using statements if not already present.

Then check what calls `IsResource<T>()` - it's called from within `ArmOperation` class. Any method calling `IsResource<T>()` needs to propagate the annotation on its own generic parameter `T`. Look for callers within the file and add the same `[DynamicallyAccessedMembers]` annotation to their generic `T` parameter as well.

## 4. GenericOperationSource.cs - Fix IL2087 (lines 37, 40)

The class `GenericOperationSource<T>` at line 16:
```csharp
internal class GenericOperationSource<T> : IOperationSource<T>
```

Line 37 uses `ModelReaderWriter.Read(response.Content, typeof(T))` and line 40 uses `Activator.CreateInstance(typeof(T), ...)`.

Add `[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.PublicConstructors | DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)]` to the class-level generic parameter `T`:
```csharp
